  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\nPost frontal precipitation and brisk conditions will persist across \nthe area through this afternoon. Some wrap around shower activity may\nlinger into tonight as a secondary cold front pivots through the \narea. In continued low level CAA, temperatures will drop into the mid\n30s to lower 40s overnight, but clouds and winds will help prevent \nfrost formation.\n\nKey Message 2) \nSurface high pressure will build into our area Saturday into \nSaturday night before beginning to shift off to the east on Sunday. \nThis will bring dry and continued cold conditions. With the surface \nhigh centered over Ohio by early Sunday morning, expect good \nradiational cooling for Saturday night, with clear skies and light \nwinds. Have undercut temps somewhat and will generally go with lows \nin the upper 20s to lower 30s, with cooler readings possible in the \nmore sheltered areas. Have issued a Freeze Watch for our entire area\nfor Saturday night into Sunday morning. \n\nBelow normal temperatures will continue on Sunday with highs in the \nupper 50s to lower 60s. We will then gradually moderate through the \nrest of next week as the surface high shifts slowly east.",
